sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as External Client
    participant Gateway as Gateway API Gateway<br/>443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    participant IPPPre as payload-processing<br/>(ipp-pre)<br/>9004/TCP gRPC mTLS
    participant Authorino as Authorino<br/>(Kuadrant AuthPolicy)<br/>mTLS
    participant MaaSAPI as maas-api<br/>8443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    participant PostgreSQL as PostgreSQL<br/>5432/TCP TLS
    participant IPP as payload-processing<br/>(ipp)<br/>9004/TCP gRPC mTLS
    participant KServe as KServe LLM Endpoint<br/>HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    participant OIDC as OpenShift/OIDC Provider<br/>443/TCP HTTPS

    rect rgb(240, 248, 255)
        Note over Client,KServe: Flow 1: Model Inference Request (API Key Auth)
        Client->>Gateway: POST /v1/models/{model}:predict<br/>Auth: Bearer sk-oai-*
        Gateway->>IPPPre: ext_proc: Extract model name<br/>from headers/body (gRPC mTLS)
        IPPPre-->>Gateway: Model name + routing headers
        Gateway->>Authorino: Auth check (gRPC mTLS)
        Authorino->>MaaSAPI: POST /internal/v1/api-keys/validate<br/>Validate key hash (network-isolated)
        MaaSAPI->>PostgreSQL: SELECT api_key WHERE hash=SHA256(key)<br/>Password auth
        PostgreSQL-->>MaaSAPI: Key record + tenant
        MaaSAPI-->>Authorino: Valid + user identity
        Authorino->>MaaSAPI: POST /internal/v1/subscriptions/select<br/>Find matching subscription
        MaaSAPI-->>Authorino: Selected subscription + rate limits
        Authorino-->>Gateway: Auth success + identity headers<br/>Strip original Authorization
        Gateway->>IPP: ext_proc: Process body<br/>(post-auth, gRPC mTLS)
        IPP-->>Gateway: Processed request
        Gateway->>KServe: Forward to model endpoint<br/>via HTTPRoute (HTTPS, cluster CA)
        KServe-->>Gateway: Inference response
        Gateway-->>Client: JSON response (HTTPS TLS 1.2+)
    end

    rect rgb(255, 248, 240)
        Note over Client,PostgreSQL: Flow 2: API Key Creation (User Token Auth)
        Client->>Gateway: POST /v1/api-keys<br/>Auth: Bearer <OIDC token>
        Gateway->>Authorino: Auth check (gRPC mTLS)
        Authorino->>OIDC: Validate token<br/>HTTPS TLS 1.2+
        OIDC-->>Authorino: Token valid + claims
        Authorino-->>Gateway: Auth success<br/>X-MaaS-Username + X-MaaS-Group headers
        Gateway->>MaaSAPI: POST /v1/api-keys<br/>HTTPS TLS 1.2+<br/>Headers: X-MaaS-Username, X-MaaS-Group
        MaaSAPI->>MaaSAPI: Generate sk-oai-* key<br/>SHA-256 hash (null-byte delim)
        MaaSAPI->>PostgreSQL: INSERT api_key hash<br/>Password auth
        PostgreSQL-->>MaaSAPI: Stored
        MaaSAPI-->>Gateway: Plaintext API key (show-once)
        Gateway-->>Client: API key response (HTTPS TLS 1.2+)
    end

    rect rgb(240, 255, 240)
        Note over Gateway,PostgreSQL: Flow 3: AITenant Reconciliation
        Note right of MaaSAPI: maas-controller watches AITenant CRs
        MaaSAPI->>MaaSAPI: maas-controller: AITenant CR event
        MaaSAPI->>Gateway: Create/validate Gateway CR<br/>HTTPS 443/TCP ServiceAccount token
        MaaSAPI->>Gateway: Create Namespace<br/>HTTPS 443/TCP ServiceAccount token
        MaaSAPI->>Gateway: Create MaasTenantConfig<br/>HTTPS 443/TCP ServiceAccount token
        MaaSAPI->>Gateway: Create Roles/RoleBindings<br/>HTTPS 443/TCP ServiceAccount token
        MaaSAPI->>Gateway: Deploy maas-api instance<br/>(Deployment, Service, NetworkPolicy, CronJob)
    end
